  "has_quantitative_results": true,
  "summary": "The paper proposes a hybrid model combining a classical encoder, a 4–12 qubit parameterized quantum circuit (depth 1–5), and a classical decoder for time-series forecasting. On simulator experiments, the hybrid model achieves MSE 0.008 vs Transformer 0.010 for electricity load, 0.014 vs 0.016 for stock prices, and 0.010 vs 0.012 for weather forecasting, with corresponding R² up to 0.94. Results are averaged over 5 runs with 5‑fold cross-validation.",
